==Notes==
*"The jacinth wakes the rising sun" is a riddle of an obscure [[Lore:Alchemy|alchemical]] formula{{Ref|name=TDOO|{{Cite Book|The Doors of Oblivion}}}} that can provide access to the [[Lore:Fields of Regret|Fields of Regret]], the domain of [[Lore:Clavicus Vile|Clavicus Vile]]. The "Rising Sun" refers to [[Lore:Orc's blood|Orc's blood]] and the "Jacinth" is [[Lore:Amber|Amber]].{{Ref|name=RGIszara|[[Redguard:Rescue Iszara|Rescue Iszara]] story quest in {{G|redguard}}}}{{Ref|name=NGS|{{Cite Book|N'Gasta's Spellbook|ns_base=RG}}}} The master conjurer, [[Lore:Morian Zenas|Morian Zenas]] labels the complete process a Door of Oblivion.{{Ref|name=TDOO}}
*Originally, the Sun was meant to set in the east and rise in the west, and the directions of east and west were intended to be reversed across the board in the ''Elder Scrolls'' setting. Remnants of this design can be found all throughout ''Arena''. Ultimately this was inconsistent throughout the game's design, and was abandoned for future titles.{{Ref|name=TedPosts|group=UOL|{{Cite Book|ns_base=General|Ted Peterson's Posts}}}} Dawn's light rising in the west is mentioned in ''[[Lore:The Legend of Lovers Lament|The Legend of Lovers Lament]]'' from ''Daggerfall'', however.{{ref|{{Cite book|The Legend of Lovers Lament}}}}

